{"ts":"2026-08-05T18:37:19.028Z","type":"finding","frontier":"startup-replica-reconciliation-sweep","claim":"Design pinned via two explore subagents + code trace: the orphaned-replica-file case (replica reassigned while node down, or crash between services-row DELETE and file unlink) is NOT covered by the existing runReplicaLifecycleRecovery, which only handles services rows in transitional states (STARTING/SYNCING/STOPPING) — a file with NO services row is invisible to it. The sweep therefore runs POST-hydration inside replica-lifecycle-recovery (where systemTableCache holds the canonical services assignment per depends-on-identity-manifest), comparing on-disk partitions/{partitionId}/{replicaId}.db files for nodes-p* partitions against services rows for this node_id: a file with no matching services row is quarantined (renamed aside, never read post-hydration) rather than deleted outright, preserving fail-closed diagnosis; a file whose row exists is untouched. Pre-hydration the raw union scan no longer exists as an authority path (startup-evidence-single-identity-decision-v2 replaced it with typed evidence), so the post-hydration sweep runs before any consumer can read the orphaned file as current evidence. Sweep keys on the canonical assignment, never on the file union (constraint sweep-keys-on-authoritative-assignment).","kind":"design","evidence":"explore:ses_02cd45d8effeDnaUx4NhP900VY","rulesOut":null,"verification":null,"regressionClassification":null,"scopePressureClassification":null}
